  "question": {
    "text": "U-tube moves with a constant speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math> parallel to the surface of a stationary liquid. The cross-section area of the lower part of the tube lowered into the liquid, is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and that of the top part located over the liquid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. Friction and formation of waves should be neglected. The density of the fluid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ρ</mi></math>. Neglect difference in heights at both the openings of the tube.<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/266333.JPG\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 212px;\" /><br />\r<br />\rThe velocity of the liquid coming out of the top part as seen by an observer on the ground will be",
    "image": null
  },
