  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Using the equation of continuity, we get<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math> (liquid is entering in pipe with a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math> with respect to the pipe)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math><br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>:</mo></math> velocity of liquid at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> with respect to pipe<br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi></math> With respect to ground, the speed of liquid will be,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
